# Entry Main. A path write of a body reaches the right-hand side of a retained declaration of the call's data: the
# declaration keeps its identity, its operand becomes the address of the written cell, its initializer is not
# executed, and the read of the place goes through to the written value. `cf_description` declares `cf_pending`
# with the computed initializer `bump()` and writes `data[0][1] := @cf_five` before returning `cf_pending`: the result
# is 5, `calls` 0 (the row of the self-test graph_call_frames, case 122; the norm; Sol and Astra).
# Norm: the book #call-frame (a local without a write back keeps its place; a reached declaration is read by what its
# operand is now), #frame-and-graph-assignment (a write through an index replaces one cell).
Counter:
    int: calls 0
end: Counter
fn: bump () int
    Counter\calls := Counter\calls + 1
    return: 9
end: bump
fn: cf_description () int (int: cf_pending bump())
    int: cf_five 5
    data[0][1] := @cf_five
    return: cf_pending
end: cf_description
int: r 0
Main:
    node\r := cf_description()
